      "id": 1,
      "text": "Smithfield became an independent town in 1731, holding its first town meeting that March at Captain Richard Whitman's home.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smithfield%2C_Rhode_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named for John Smith, “The Miller,” who received land from Roger Williams and helped found Providence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.smithfieldri.gov/our-town/town-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the Industrial Revolution, Smithfield evolved from a farming community into a textile hub with mills along the Woonasquatucket River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smithfield%2C_Rhode_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Quakers in Smithfield were early abolitionists; Effingham Capron and Abby Kelley Foster were among those who fought for freedom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smithfield%2C_Rhode_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Bryant University, a private four‑year college, sits in Smithfield and attracts students from across the country.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
